e5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-136413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(9i-64j)\\,\\text{mm}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/state.json" "file_sha256" "348c86b40af16516a99a035564bfa9fcff6796a53b3c91ee5e5028bbc5812198" "basis" 1425 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040268/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A delivery drone starts from the point with position vector $(1i+2j)\\,\\text{mi}$ and moves with a constant velocity of $(3i-2j)\\,\\text{mi/h}.$ Determine the distance $(|r|)$ from the drone to the origin after $3$ hours.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{mi}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a23c0613d8993213ca657c3259e3042158734c32e84a24eb887b22ee3d1f9b4" "basis" 1852 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=1i+2j,\\,u=3i-2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the drone after $t=3\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(1i+2j)+(3i-2j)(3) \\\\  & =(1i+2j)+(9i-6j) \\\\  & =(10i-4j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the drone to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|10i-4j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{116} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{29}\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a23c0613d8993213ca657c3259e3042158734c32e84a24eb887b22ee3d1f9b4" "basis" 1852 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c10ab3b8de38e019ed732ed5c94060ef7940d5e7a67cdfab8e1b377c7097ee38" "basis" 1852 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280521" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a23c0613d8993213ca657c3259e3042158734c32e84a24eb887b22ee3d1f9b4" "basis" 1852 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "An object moves from the origin with an acceleration of $(-2i+4j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(3i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the distance from the object to the origin$(|r|)$ after $2$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a23c0613d8993213ca657c3259e3042158734c32e84a24eb887b22ee3d1f9b4" "basis" 1852 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=3i+j,\\,a=-2i+4j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the object after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(3i+j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2i+4j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(6i+2j)+\\frac{1}{2}(-8i+16j) \\\\  & =(6i+2j)+(-4i+8j) \\\\  & =(2i+10j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the object to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|2i+10j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{104} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{26}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a23c0613d8993213ca657c3259e3042158734c32e84a24eb887b22ee3d1f9b4" "basis" 1852 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c10ab3b8de38e019ed732ed5c94060ef7940d5e7a67cdfab8e1b377c7097ee38" "basis" 1852 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280533" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a23c0613d8993213ca657c3259e3042158734c32e84a24eb887b22ee3d1f9b4" "basis" 1852 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280533" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{26}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a23c0613d8993213ca657c3259e3042158734c32e84a24eb887b22ee3d1f9b4" "basis" 1852 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057503/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-136413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(-i+j)\\,\\text{mm}$ with an acceleration of $(2i-6j)\\,{\\text{mm/min}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(-3i+2j)\\,\\text{mm/min}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $5$ minutes." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-136413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=-i+j,\\,u=-3i+2j,\\,a=2i-6j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=5\\,\\text{min}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(-i+j)+(-3i+2j)(5)+\\frac{1}{2}(2i-6j)(5)^{2} \\\\  & =(-i+j)+(-15i+10j)+25(i-3j) \\\\  & =(-16i+11j)+(25i-75j) \\\\  & =(9i-64j)\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-136413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a67421a46cd509c369e81d29da97732c89ed3c2ce9738f037c6bf70a23718ae"} {"question" "q-136413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-136413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(16i+49j)\\,\\text{mm}"] ["math" "(25i+36j)\\,\\text{mm}"] ["math" "(3i-8j)\\,\\text{mm}"] ["math" "(4i-7j)\\,\\text{mm}"] ["math" "(9i-64j)\\,\\text{mm}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-136413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(9i-64j)\\,\\text{mm}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-136421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves from the origin with an acceleration of $(-i+3j)\\,{\\text{cm/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(4i+j)\\,\\text{cm/s}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $2$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-136421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=4i+j,\\,a=-i+3j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(4i+j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(-i+3j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(8i+2j)+2(-i+3j) \\\\  & =(8i+2j)+(-2i+6j) \\\\  & =(6i+8j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-136421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a67421a46cd509c369e81d29da97732c89ed3c2ce9738f037c6bf70a23718ae"} {"question" "q-136421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-136421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2i+3j)\\,\\text{cm}"] ["math" "(-i+7j)\\,\\text{cm}"] ["math" "(3i-2j)\\,\\text{cm}"] ["math" "(5i+4j)\\,\\text{cm}"] ["math" "(6i+8j)\\,\\text{cm}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-136421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(6i+8j)\\,\\text{cm}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-280507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A toy rocket is launched from the origin with an initial velocity of $(2i+6j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ and a constant acceleration of $(i+5j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Determine the position vector of the rocket after $2$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{m}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-280507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=2i+6j,\\,a=i+5j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the rocket after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(2i+6j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+5j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(4i+12j)+2(i+5j) \\\\  & =(4i+12j)+(2i+10j) \\\\  & =(\\,6\\,i+22\\,j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-280507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a67421a46cd509c369e81d29da97732c89ed3c2ce9738f037c6bf70a23718ae"} {"question" "q-280507" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-280507" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-280507" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-280507" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "22"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-280521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A delivery drone starts from the point with position vector $(1i+2j)\\,\\text{mi}$ and moves with a constant velocity of $(3i-2j)\\,\\text{mi/h}.$ Determine the distance $(|r|)$ from the drone to the origin after $3$ hours.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{mi}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-280521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=1i+2j,\\,u=3i-2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the drone after $t=3\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(1i+2j)+(3i-2j)(3) \\\\  & =(1i+2j)+(9i-6j) \\\\  & =(10i-4j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the drone to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|10i-4j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{116} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{29}\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-280521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a67421a46cd509c369e81d29da97732c89ed3c2ce9738f037c6bf70a23718ae"} {"question" "q-280521" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-280521" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{29}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-280533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "An object moves from the origin with an acceleration of $(-2i+4j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(3i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the distance from the object to the origin$(|r|)$ after $2$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-280533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=3i+j,\\,a=-2i+4j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the object after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(3i+j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2i+4j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(6i+2j)+\\frac{1}{2}(-8i+16j) \\\\  & =(6i+2j)+(-4i+8j) \\\\  & =(2i+10j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the object to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|2i+10j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{104} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{26}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-280533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a67421a46cd509c369e81d29da97732c89ed3c2ce9738f037c6bf70a23718ae"} {"question" "q-280533" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"} {"question" "q-280533" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{26}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071606/state.json" "file_sha256" "a41575cc8172eafd7545e68911e15552ec3d1c54945fd9fba1c59e0bfc616c58"}] "usage" {"q-136413" [] "q-280533" [] "q-280521" [] "q-280507" []} "basis" 2585 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186306651 17592186306652 17592186306653 17592186306654 17592186306655 17592186306700 17592186306701 17592186306703 17592186334888 17592186334889 17592186334892] "immutable_fields" [[17592186306650 :answer-field/correct] [17592186306650 :answer-field/id] [17592186306650 :answer-field/key] [17592186306650 :answer-field/type] [17592186306699 :answer-field/correct] [17592186306699 :answer-field/id] [17592186306699 :answer-field/key] [17592186306699 :answer-fiel